  "body": "Follows https://github.com/heycam/webidl/pull/906. Non-mechanical\nchanges:\n\n* An example IDL interface listing was using an \"in\" argument, which\n  seemed unnecessarily divergent from actual Web IDL. Removed that.\n\n* Updated customElements.get() to have a more precise return type now\n  that it is possible. Also updated the custom element definition\n  struct's constructor item to be a CustomElementConstructor instead of\n  a Function; that was missed in #3703.\n\n---\n\nI am *pretty sure* I didn't actually replace any non-IDL instances of \"void\" with \"undefined\" (e.g. \"void element\"). I checked it over manually a few times. But a second set of eyes would be helpful.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5838/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 17, 2020, 6:35 PM UTC (b697c42)\">/canvas.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5838/3729254...b697c42/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 17, 2020, 6:35 PM UTC (b697c42)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5838/common-dom-interfaces.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 17, 2020, 6:35 PM UTC (b697c42)\">/common-dom-interfaces.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5838/3729254...b697c42/common-dom-interfaces.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 17, 2020, 6:35 PM UTC (b697c42)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5838/comms.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 17, 2020, 6:35 PM UTC (b697c42)\">/comms.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5838/3729254...b697c42/comms.html\" title=\"Last updated on Aug 17, 20